@@ -26,12 +26,16 @@ All product endpoints are JSON endpoints under `/api/v1`. Requests other than ac
 
 Customers register at `POST /api/v1/registrations`, then use the standard verification and session endpoints. Authenticated customers use `/api/v1/requests` and its nested `/comments` route; staff use `/api/v1/tickets`. Replies, status changes, and active-staff assignments are submitted with `PATCH`. Private staff comments are excluded from customer comment responses and do not touch the customer request timestamp. Lists accept `page` and `per_page` and include pagination metadata with the records.
 
-Staff can set each ticket's `priority` to `normal` (the default) or `high`. Staff ticket responses include priority, while customer request responses do not. Staff can combine `status`, `assignee_id`, `requester_id`, `priority`, and `q` filters on `/api/v1/tickets`; `assignee_id=unassigned` selects tickets without an assignee. `q` is a case-insensitive literal search of subjects and public comments. Customer request lists support only the `status` filter.
+Staff can set each ticket's `priority` to `normal` (the default) or `high`. Staff ticket responses include priority, while customer request responses do not. Staff can combine `status`, `assignee_id`, `group_id`, `requester_id`, `priority`, and `q` filters on `/api/v1/tickets`; `assignee_id=unassigned` selects tickets without an assignee. `q` is a case-insensitive literal search of subjects and public comments. Customer request lists support only the `status` filter.
 
 Admins manage staff invitations through `/api/v1/invitations`, including list/show, `POST /api/v1/invitations/:id/resend`, and `DELETE /api/v1/invitations/:id`. Invitations expire after seven days. The frontend previews a token with `POST /invitation_previews` (also available at `/api/v1/invitation_previews`) and accepts it at `POST /api/v1/invitation_acceptances`. Accepted staff are verified immediately.
 
 Admins list and inspect users at `/api/v1/users` and update roles or suspension at `/api/v1/users/:id`. User lists can filter by `role` and `suspended`. `GET /api/v1/staff` returns all active admin and agent choices for ticket assignment. Suspending a user revokes their sessions and clears their ticket assignments; the last active admin cannot be suspended or demoted.
 
+Staff can browse `/api/v1/groups` and `/api/v1/group_memberships`; only admins can create, rename, or delete groups and manage memberships. A staff member can belong to multiple groups, and membership lists can be filtered by `group_id` and `user_id`. Every staff member with memberships has one default; set it with `PUT /api/v1/group_memberships/:id/make_default`. Removing a default membership promotes another membership automatically. Suspension retains memberships, while demotion removes them.
+
+Staff ticket responses include `group_id` and a `group` object containing the ID and name. `/api/v1/tickets` accepts a numeric `group_id` or `group_id=unassigned`. Assignees must belong to the selected group. Assigning an otherwise ungrouped ticket uses the staff member's default group; moving a ticket to another group clears an incompatible assignee. Clearing `assignee_id` retains the group, while explicitly clearing `group_id` also clears the assignee.
+
 Verification and password-reset emails contain links to the configured frontend URL. The confirmation API endpoints are `/api/v1/email_verifications/confirm` and `/api/v1/password_resets/confirm`.
 
